10.1128/jvi.01714-18,f8c599bb24ccfef4,0,10.1128/JVI.78.19.10765-10775.2004,Temporal modulation of an autoprotease is crucial for replication and pathogenicity of an RNA virus.,"Lackner T, Müller A, Pankraz A, Becher P, Thiel H-J, Gorbalenya AE, Tautz N.",2004,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Lackner T, Müller A, Pankraz A, Becher P, Thiel H-J, Gorbalenya AE, Tautz N."", ""year"": ""2004"", ""title"": ""Temporal modulation of an autoprotease is crucial for replication and pathogenicity of an RNA virus."", ""doi"": ""10.1128/JVI.78.19.10765-10775.2004"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The observation that the NS2-5B/NCP7 WT replicon exhibited a lower replication efficiency than the NS2-5B/CP7 WT replicon in naive MDBK cells at 24 h and 48 hpe argues that the DNAJC14-mediated temporal regulation mechanism of NS2-3 cleavage during the replication of the NS2-5B/NCP7 WT replicon contributes to this lower replication efficiency and is in line with the lower RNA replication efficiency known for NCP7 infections than CP7 infections (14)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The observation that the NS2-5B/NCP7 WT replicon exhibited a lower replication efficiency than the NS2-5B/CP7 WT replicon in naive MDBK cells at 24 h and 48 hpe argues that the DNAJC14-mediated temporal regulation mechanism of NS2-3 cleavage during the replication of the NS2-5B/NCP7 WT replicon contributes to this lower replication efficiency and is in line with the lower RNA replication efficiency known for NCP7 infections than CP7 infections (14)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The new replicon experiment explicitly compares and agrees with the reported NCP7-versus-CP7 RNA replication difference.""}"
10.1128/jvi.01714-18,f8c599bb24ccfef4,2,10.1073/pnas.0508247103,Dissection of a viral autoprotease elucidates a function of a cellular chaperone in proteolysis.,"Lackner T, Thiel H-J, Tautz N.",2006,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Lackner T, Thiel H-J, Tautz N."", ""year"": ""2006"", ""title"": ""Dissection of a viral autoprotease elucidates a function of a cellular chaperone in proteolysis."", ""doi"": ""10.1073/pnas.0508247103"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Our experiments reemphasize that, mechanistically, the cochaperone function of the DNAJC14 J-domain (essential for the association between J-domain proteins with chaperones of the Hsp70 family [85]) is not required for NS2 activation, as proposed earlier (53)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Our experiments reemphasize that, mechanistically, the cochaperone function of the DNAJC14 J-domain (essential for the association between J-domain proteins with chaperones of the Hsp70 family [85]) is not required for NS2 activation, as proposed earlier (53)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The isolated-domain rescue tests whether the previously reported NS2 activation operates without the cochaperone J-domain. Authors explicitly confirm the specific earlier proposal.""}"
10.1080/00223891.2018.1539004,6a3af07d1dcf7c08,1,,Short and extra-short forms of the Big Five Inventory–2: The BFI-2-S and BFI-2-XS.,"Soto, C. J., & John, O. P.",2017,full_text,competing_supported_matches; same_author_year_siblings,correct,argon,"{""target_index"": 1, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""shipped_right"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""Besides the 60-item version, Soto and John (2017a) published short (30-item) and extra-short (15-item) versions of the BFI–2, with acceptable to good reliabilities for short Big Five domain scales. Table 2 also displays the Cronbach’s alphas of these shorter scales in the Dutch adaptation."", ""location"": ""Study 1, Results, Reliability analysis, p. 315"", ""reason"": ""Not an omitted target (materials/measure citation only). The authors administered the 60-item BFI-2 to replicate Soto and John (2017b) and only cited the sibling paper Soto and John (2017a) in a single paragraph of Study 1's reliability analysis to define the 30-item and 15-item subsets scored for descriptive Cronbach's alphas in Table 2, without testing their structure or validity or framing Soto and John (2017a) as a replication target in the study aims or conclusion.""}","{""authors"": ""Soto, C. J., & John, O. P."", ""year"": ""2017"", ""title"": ""Short and extra-short forms of the Big Five Inventory–2: The BFI-2-S and BFI-2-XS."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Besides the 60-item version, Soto and John (2017a) published short (30-item) and extra-short (15-item) versions of\nthe BFI–2, with acceptable to good reliabilities for short Big\nFive domain scales. Table 2 also displays the Cronbach’s\nalphas of these shorter scales in the Dutch adaptation."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The 60-item BFI–2 was\nreliable at the level of both domains and facets, as were the abbreviated versions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abbreviated forms were explicitly re-evaluated and described as reliable; weaker internal consistencies alone do not imply failure.""}"
