10.1177/0016986220932533,fc67e05e8823cd82,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Terman’s study was the first to systematically document the lives of the intellectually gifted. This cross-sectional study replicates and extends some of Terman’s findings on characteristics of the gifted in childhood, comparing largely unselected samples of gifted ( n = 50) and average-ability ( n = 50) adolescents matched by means of propensity score matching."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Results support Terman’s findings on gifted individuals’ psychological functioning and contradict negative stereotypes about the gifted."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract explicitly supports Terman’s findings. The particular original publication cannot be distinguished from the abstract.""}"
