10.1017/s0261444818000368,259ed3faa8c43fba,5,10.1017/S0272263103000044,Constraints on ‘noticing the gap.’,"Philp, J.",2003,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Philp, J."", ""year"": ""2003"", ""title"": ""Constraints on ‘noticing the gap.’"", ""doi"": ""10.1017/S0272263103000044"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Unlike prior research though, the current dataset failed to confirm the effect of recast length whereby shorter recasts have been more frequently noticed (Philp 2003) or recognized as being corrective (Egi 2007) and have elicited higher repair rates (Sheen 2006)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Unlike prior research though, the current dataset failed to confirm the effect of recast length whereby shorter recasts have been more frequently noticed (Philp 2003) or recognized as being corrective (Egi 2007) and have elicited higher repair rates (Sheen 2006)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly state failure to confirm the shorter-recast effect in their current data and name this original within the comparison. DOI copied as printed, without repairing typographical errors.""}"
