10.1080/19345747.2024.2333734,865e547d45f851f6,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The On Track program, previously found to be effective in a researcher-driven and tightly controlled setting, was implemented in a larger sample of schools. To investigate the robustness of the original findings, specific aspects of the implementation were deliberately altered from the original study."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Results indicated that the intervention significantly reduced the number of at-risk students by the end of first grade. However, effect sizes in the replication study were reduced compared to the original try-out."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Abstract states original program effective and corresponding beneficial intervention result, explicitly compares reduced sizes; reduced magnitude alone is not mixed. Reference citation is not in the abstract.""}"
10.24839/2325-7342.jn26.4.422,4b693b1501136919,1,10.1027/1864-1105/a000036,"“I really liked that movie”: Testing the relationship between trait empathy, transportation, perceived realism, and movie enjoyment.","Hall, A. E., & Bracken, C. C.",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Hall, A. E., & Bracken, C. C."", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""“I really liked that movie”: Testing the relationship between trait empathy, transportation, perceived realism, and movie enjoyment."", ""doi"": ""10.1027/1864-1105/a000036"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The first hypothesis was that trait empathy would be positively correlated with narrative transportation (Hall & Bracken, 2011; Taylor, 2015)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The correlation detected between trait empathy and narrative transportation supports and extends prior literature that has demonstrated similar results with films (Hall & Bracken, 2011; Taylor, 2015), as well as studies that have examined the relationship between some components of trait empathy and narrative transportation into written pieces (Bal & Veltkamp, 2013; Johnson, 2012)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Explicit discussion comparison settles this published finding.""}"
