10.1177/08902070221094216,4f26155990969ba5,1,10.2139/ssrn.1804189,Measuring social value orientation.,"Murphy, R. O., Ackermann, K. A., & Handgraaf, M. J. J.",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Murphy, R. O., Ackermann, K. A., & Handgraaf, M. J. J."", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""Measuring social value orientation."", ""doi"": ""10.2139/ssrn.1804189"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""It serves as a replication of earlier research (i.e., Murphy et al., 2011) that, with a somewhat small sample size, it showed a fair but no strong correspondence between these two measures; and it helps us to explore whether the associations with attachment, number of siblings, and age are similar for the two measures."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We found only a medium-sized correspondence between the two measurements, accounting for a shared variance of about 50%, and around 75% percent of participants were classified into the same SVO category. This is consistent with earlier findings (e.g., Bakker & Dijkstra, 2021; Matsumoto et al., 2016; Murphy et al., 2011), and so it is fair to conclude that the two measures are both similar and distinct."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.1080/02699931.2018.1504747,10bf96c2e0226ded,1,,Counterfactual thinking and victim compensation: A test of norm theory.,"Miller, D. T., & McFarland, C.",1986,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""authors"": ""Miller, D. T., & McFarland, C."", ""year"": ""1986"", ""title"": ""Counterfactual thinking and victim compensation: A test of norm theory."", ""study_numbers"": ""1"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Part 3 is a replication of Experiment 1 from Miller and McFarland (1986) with the robbery-scenario – the study that meant to provide the ﬁrst empirical test of norm theory."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The robbery scenario (Miller & McFarland, 1986) failed to replicate using the original experimental paradigm using a compensation measure, yet we found support for an exceptionality eﬀect using an added measure of perceived regret."", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Explicit failure verdict on original compensation finding. Positive perceived-regret finding is an added extension and does not confirm the original compensation result.""}"
10.1371/journal.pone.0147770,569d8454dfe97d14,1,,The stability of working memory: Do previous tasks influence complex span?,"Healey MK, Hasher L, Danilova E",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Healey MK, Hasher L, Danilova E"", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""The stability of working memory: Do previous tasks influence complex span?"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In this study, for the depletion task, we used the actual video material and verbatim instructions from the popular video-viewing attention control task employed by prior researchers. For the outcome task, we used a complex working memory span task known as the operation span task (OSPAN; [\n36\n]). We selected these particular tasks because they maximize the chances of demonstrating the ego-depletion effect for the following reasons: a) the video-viewing attention control task is one of the most widely used tasks and has consistently been shown to induce ego-depletion in prior research (e.g., [\n5\n,\n31\n–\n33\n]); b) the OSPAN task places heavy demand on executive attention and hence should tax self-control resources (e.g., [\n37\n]); c) this particular combination of tasks has produced medium to large effect sizes in prior studies [\n5\n,\n38\n]; d) these tasks are matched in terms of stimulus modality (i.e., both tasks utilize words), which has been shown to amplify the ego-depletion effect [\n38\n]. "", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Contrary to the ego-depletion hypothesis, participants in the depletion condition did not perform worse than control participants on the subsequent self-control task, even after considering moderator variables."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The task combination is explicitly linked to these two prior effect demonstrations; the present attempt finds no depletion effect.""}"
10.1037/xhp0000489,b371e50524c8b0ba,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""In Experiments 1 and 2, we replicate our results using a stimulus setup that made random sampling unlikely."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In Experiments 1 and 2, we replicate our results using a stimulus setup that made random sampling unlikely."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract explicitly says Experiments 1 and 2 replicate the prior results. The prior paper citation cannot be extracted from this abstract.""}"
10.1111/pops.12446,1c45a16ad2fefb39,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""An initial study analyzing two small‐scale field experiments argued that describing someone as a voter (noun) instead of one who votes (verb) increases turnout rates 11 to 14 points because the noun activates a person's social identity as a voter."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We find no evidence that this minor wording change increases turnout levels."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Abstract states the original positive noun-versus-verb turnout finding and this replication finds no evidence of the increase.""}"
10.1080/02699931.2020.1863187,67d37622e14f4554,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2, 3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""However, because we did not replicate the mnemonic advantage of disgust, subsequent experiments were concerned with testing the replicability of this effect."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Because metamemorial judgments sometimes eliminate memory effects, participants in Experiment 2 did not make such judgments. Even so, the effect did not replicate. The disgust advantage was ultimately replicated in Experiment 3, where participants completed a secondary task at encoding."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly report failures in Experiments 1 and 2 and replication in Experiment 3. The concluding statement calls the advantage replicable but less robust; the reported studies have conflicting results. Target citation is absent from the available abstract.""}"
10.1080/10584609809342367,465e6cc7a6102b55,0,,,"Roberts, Marilyn; McCombs, Maxwell",,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Roberts, Marilyn; McCombs, Maxwell"", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This study had two goals: to replicate research by Marilyn Roberts and Maxwell McCombs on intermedia agenda setting in a Spanish election and to explore that pattern of intermedia relationships at both the first and second levels of agenda setting."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Similar to Roberts and McCombs' findings in a Texas gubernatorial election, the newspaper agenda in Spain did influence the agenda of issues in television news."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract explicitly compares the newspaper-to-television agenda result with the target and reports agreement. The reference list is unavailable, so target title and year are left blank.""}"
10.1016/j.bbr.2024.115096,a23c52a8487df33f,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""A previous study with Virtual Reality (VR) and online motion-capture quantified this approach bias towards food and non-food cues in a controlled VR environment with hand movements. The aim of this study was to test the specificity of a manual approach bias for high-calorie food in grasp movements compared to low-calorie food and neutral objects of different complexity, namely, simple balls and geometrically more complex office tools."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The results confirm the presence of bottom-up advantages in motor-cognitive behaviour for high-calorie food in a non-clinical population."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Abstract states the earlier approach bias and confirms the corresponding high-calorie approach advantage. Citation unavailable in abstract.""}"
