10.23668/psycharchives.4766,3617489aca51758c,7,10.1177/0022487117702580,Preservice to inservice: Does mathematics anxiety change with teaching experience?,"Gresham, G.",2018,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Gresham, G."", ""year"": ""2018"", ""title"": ""Preservice to inservice: Does mathematics anxiety change with teaching experience?"", ""doi"": ""10.1177/0022487117702580"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Consistent with this reported decrease in math anxiety during teacher education, Gresham (2018) found evidence for a further decrease in math anxiety when teachers start teaching. Our study, however, does not support these previously found differences and instead provides moderate evidence for similar levels of math anxiety for female pre-service and in-service elementary school teachers, even when specialization in math was taken into account."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Consistent with this reported decrease in math anxiety during teacher education, Gresham (2018) found evidence for a further decrease in math anxiety when teachers start teaching. Our study, however, does not support these previously found differences and instead provides moderate evidence for similar levels of math anxiety for female pre-service and in-service elementary school teachers, even when specialization in math was taken into account."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly compare their own result with this cited original finding. The stated agreement or disagreement determines this target’s outcome.""}"
