10.1016/j.euroecorev.2015.05.006,6986d6215bbf814f,1,,"The willingness to pay–willingness to accept gap, the “Endowment Effect,” subject misconceptions, and experimental procedures for eliciting valuations: comment.","Isoni, Andrea, Loomes, Graham, Sugden, Robert",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Isoni, Andrea, Loomes, Graham, Sugden, Robert"", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""The willingness to pay–willingness to accept gap, the “Endowment Effect,” subject misconceptions, and experimental procedures for eliciting valuations: comment."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""While we replicate the experiments of PZ and ILS as closely as possible and use features of their setup to identify subject misconceptions, Bartling et al. (forthcoming) focus on the claim in Cason and Plott (2014) that misconceptions about the BDM can be falsely interpreted as support for theories of framing, such as reference-dependent preferences."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Thus, we are not able to replicate the results on the valuations of mugs by PZ and ILS."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Explicit failure verdict for the central mug valuation finding. Agreement in training lottery tasks does not overturn the failure of the focal effect.""}"
https://openalex.org/w96171599,85d1ad39a05d633c,1,10.1038/ng.664,A genome-wide association study for myopia and refractive error identifies a susceptibility locus at 15q25.,"Hysi PG, Young TL, Mackey DA, Andrew T, Fernandez-Medarde A, Solouki AM, Hewitt AW, Macgregor S, Vingerling JR, Li YJ, Ikram MK, Fai LY, Sham PC, Manyes L, Porteros A, Lopes MC, Carbonaro F, Fahy SJ, Martin NG, van Duijn CM, Spector TD, Rahi JS, Santos E, Klaver CC, Hammond CJ",2010,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Hysi PG, Young TL, Mackey DA, Andrew T, Fernandez-Medarde A, Solouki AM, Hewitt AW, Macgregor S, Vingerling JR, Li YJ, Ikram MK, Fai LY, Sham PC, Manyes L, Porteros A, Lopes MC, Carbonaro F, Fahy SJ, Martin NG, van Duijn CM, Spector TD, Rahi JS, Santos E, Klaver CC, Hammond CJ"", ""year"": ""2010"", ""title"": ""A genome-wide association study for myopia and refractive error identifies a susceptibility locus at 15q25."", ""doi"": ""10.1038/ng.664"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We used the Age-Related Eye Disease Study (AREDS) cohort to replicate published significant associations at two loci on chromosome 15 from two genome-wide association studies (GWASs)."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Although use of the same SNPs used in the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia study did not show any evidence of association with refractive error in this AREDS sample, other SNPs within the candidate regions demonstrated an association with refractive error. Significant evidence of association was found using the hyperopia categorical trait, with the most significant SNPs rs1357179 on 15q14 (p=1.69×10 −3 ) and rs7164400 on 15q25 (p=8.39×10 −4 ), which passed the replication thresholds."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors contrast non-replication of the original SNPs with regional replication for hyperopia at this locus.""}"
