10.36948/ijfmr.2025.v07i06.61995,c2ce02faa87b6213,0,,,,2013,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This study conducted a direct replication of Dzulkifli and Mustafar (2013) in an Indian university population."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""This direct replication of Dzulkifli and Mustafar (2013) failed to detect significant effects of colour priming on memory span or sustained attention in a sample of 60 Indian university undergraduates. Warm colour (red) background did not enhance cognitive performance relative to cool colour (blue) or white control conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly report failure to detect the two predicted effects. Low power is discussed, but authors explicitly say their null findings are informative. Target citation is unresolved because the sole Dzulkifli/Mustafar entry is a review, not the empirical primary study attributed in the prose.""}"
https://blogs.lse.ac.uk/impactofsocialsciences/2013/09/10/bias-at-the-bbc-replicating-the-cps-analysis/,ed4df17dff750947,0,,Bias at the Beeb: A quantitative study of slant in BBC online reporting,,,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": ""Bias at the Beeb: A quantitative study of slant in BBC online reporting"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In order to dig deeper into the results obtained by the CPS, I have tried to replicate this part of the\n   research. Of course, without access to the CPS dataset there will be some differences from their\n   results, but the methodology I have applied is designed to be transparent and robust in its own\n   right."", ""outcome"": ""statistically successful but flawed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""These numbers are all indicative, prior to any reliability testing, and, of course, they do not\n   realistically provide evidence of the existence or absence of bias in the BBC any more than the\n   CPS figures do. What they do represent is a fairly simple way to debunk the main conclusions\n   drawn by the CPS from their own analysis and then spread by an overly­credulous press."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The contextualisation effects were recovered, but the main argument is that those measures do not establish ideological bias; the report’s overall interpretation is undermined.""}"
https://osf.io/wgznk,ddeb7a5f2b2f89e8,0,,,,2017,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": ""2017"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Claim for Review – The claim selected was that strongly tied customers who complain (vs. withhold feedback) after a service failure will increase their loyalty. In contrast, for weakly tied customers, complaining has no effect on loyalty."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Stage 2: H* was not supported as the interaction term on the overall ANOVA was not significant. In addition, the pattern of means in the strong ties group was not consistent but the pattern of means in the weak ties group was consistent."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Both completed stages explicitly reject support for the focal interaction. A consistent weak-ties mean pattern is ancillary to the central failed test. The final report identifies the target by project shorthand, but supplies no reference entry.""}"
https://openalex.org/w1703767599,adb4867dd3755f27,1,,,Rothermund & Wentura,2004,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Rothermund & Wentura"", ""year"": ""2004"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""However, the construct validity of this type of IAT has been called into question by recent findings showing that the IAT score implying in-group preference is rather driven by the salience asymmetry within each categorical dyad of the procedure than by evaluative associations between concepts (Rothermund & Wentura, 2001, 2004)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Consistent with our predictions, results showed that in both cases salience asymmetries reliably predict the IAT effect."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract identifies both earlier salience-asymmetry findings and reports the corresponding predicted relationship in both new experiments. Bibliographic titles and original study numbers are absent from the abstract.""}"
https://hdl.handle.net/10419/280434,a00f5635a03e4c69,0,,The origin of the state: Land productivity or appropriability?,"Mayshar, J., Moav, O., and Pascali, L.",2022,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Mayshar, J., Moav, O., and Pascali, L."", ""year"": ""2022"", ""title"": ""The origin of the state: Land productivity or appropriability?"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This is a replication of Mayshar et al. (2022) (henceforth MMP)."", ""outcome"": """", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""fulltext"", ""outcome_computation"": ""computationally reproducible"", ""outcome_computational_quote"": ""The computational reproduction of Mayshar et al. (2022) confirms that their data and code closely reproduce the main results presented in their Table 1."", ""outcome_robustness"": ""robustness challenges"", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": ""Our robustness replication with a range of plausible alternative specifications points to additional nuance and sometimes eroded support for the main results."", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors confirm close numerical reproduction, treating small discrepancies as not changing qualitative interpretation. Alternative specifications erode support and sometimes contradict central claims. Both axes concern original data; added climate controls do not constitute a fresh participant sample.""}"
